No time to delve into the big and serious music apps?
PixiTracker is what you need! It is a simple and fun tool to quickly create musical sketches, chiptunes and sound experiments. Without requiring a lot of musical knowledge!

[ Key features ]
 • true warm pixel interface;
 • pattern-based sequencer (tracker) with high quality sampler;
 • several packs with unique sounds;
 • sound recorder (from microphone or line-in);
 • MIDI keyboard support;
 • WAV export/import;
 • export to XM - this file can be loaded by any modern music tracker/player (for example, SunVox);
 • Wi-Fi export/import, iTunes File Sharing, audio copy/paste;
 • Audiobus and IAA support;
 • PixiTracker is also available for other systems (see the site);
 • PixiTracker player is open source, so you can freely use it in your own Pixilang applications.

"笙Time" is a "笙(Sho)" simulator.
"笙(Sho)" is traditional Japanese instrument for "雅楽(Gagaku - Japanese traditional music)"
It has thin 17 bamboo pipes. It sounds like small pipe organ.

Each button play blow notes.
( ' means upper octave notes)

"乞" : { A, E, A', B', E', F#' }
"一" : { B, D, E, A', B', F#' }
"工" : { C#, D, E, G#, A', B' }
"凢" : { D, E, A', B', E', F#' }
"乙" : { E, A', B', D', E', F#' }
"下" : { F#, G#, A', B', D', F#' }
"十" : { F#, G, A', B', D', E' }
"美" : { G#, A', B', C', D', F#' }
"行" : { A', B', D', E',  F#' }
"比" : { A', B', C', D', E', F#' }

Each note is not on "Equal Temperament", but on "Pure Temperament" or "Pythagorean Temperament".
Also the default base key A=430Hz

Tilting your phone, the playing volume change.
Push a button and drag your finger to out of the button, then the note can be hold. 

Setting view can set below parameters.
- Available fingering mode
  "Sho" has limit fingerings. If you want to use all button, set this mode off.
- Attack and Release Envelope
   You can set envelope time (0 to 1000 ms)
- Tone Color
   You can select tone color (Hard/Medium/Soft)
